# iris-watchdog - outside-of-me watchdog (scripts/server/iris_watchdog.py): wedge -> restart flag,
# down -> Discord DM to Zeke. 2026-10-07 hardening pass.
# 2026-10-29 code review: TimeoutStartSec so one hang under memory pressure can't wedge the oneshot (the
# timer never re-fires a unit that is still "activating"); every subprocess in the script has a timeout too.
# OOMScoreAdjust=-900 was asked for but a USER unit can't lower its own score (measured 10-29: silently
# stays 0) - that would need the root iris-oom-protect helper, which is Zeke's 10-11 OOM policy. Not here.
[Unit]
Description=Iris server watchdog (wedge restart + down alerts)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/IRIS
ExecStart=%h/venvs/iris-v100/bin/python %h/IRIS/scripts/server/iris_watchdog.py
TimeoutStartSec=90
